[{:db/id "q-36754/selection/c9dbb8199039a267dc55f6f7988962ec7f673c76d8a6d36078f852119f0595bb" :answer/id #uuid "d78e9b94-7053-513c-889e-9ac4ee996a7f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨0,\\,0,\\,2⟩+t\\,⟨0,\\,0,\\,1⟩,\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-36754/selection/c04b5bb5b1767bc9bc0a0f7233f944df6ee218e436b739becb5806a8474357da" :answer/id #uuid "03cd2d07-59f1-5c9d-909e-2170951b37aa" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨0,\\,0,\\,1⟩+t\\,⟨0,\\,0,\\,1⟩,\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-36754/selection/e9d21781d3bdf1d6d9cbe761e0321b838ab6af049a14fd085e62c095f008173d" :answer/id #uuid "c8c38b2c-71a1-501f-83d1-68f8363a1b65" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨0,\\,0,\\,-2⟩+t\\,⟨1,\\,0,\\,1⟩,\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-36754/selection/dbaa09240685cbab70733d16ceb7035bbb6c403a93b2ca40949eaf81062d92a8" :answer/id #uuid "16b5ac7f-7e44-532e-9c98-2ab0811a023b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨0,\\,0,\\,1⟩+t\\,⟨0,\\,0,\\,2⟩,\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-36754/selection/dec9d6ec669c20ec828f8233129ad1cee3d2e1ac03980852df5f2089a714a9cb" :answer/id #uuid "b1be908a-3ae9-5e12-9823-793330a24909" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨0,\\,0,\\,2⟩+t\\,⟨0,\\,-1,\\,1⟩,\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-36754/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "6f3b0ae0-9f9e-5e3a-9686-db4660f93548" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-36754/selection/c9dbb8199039a267dc55f6f7988962ec7f673c76d8a6d36078f852119f0595bb" :answer-field/choices ["q-36754/selection/c9dbb8199039a267dc55f6f7988962ec7f673c76d8a6d36078f852119f0595bb" "q-36754/selection/c04b5bb5b1767bc9bc0a0f7233f944df6ee218e436b739becb5806a8474357da" "q-36754/selection/e9d21781d3bdf1d6d9cbe761e0321b838ab6af049a14fd085e62c095f008173d" "q-36754/selection/dbaa09240685cbab70733d16ceb7035bbb6c403a93b2ca40949eaf81062d92a8" "q-36754/selection/dec9d6ec669c20ec828f8233129ad1cee3d2e1ac03980852df5f2089a714a9cb"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-36754" :question/id #uuid "a7c74ce4-3c4e-5ea4-ab88-89558065f279" :question/math-academy-id "q-36754" :question/problem "Find a vector equation of the normal line to the surface ${x}^{2}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{9}+\\frac{{z}^{2}}{4}=1$ at the point $(0,0,2).$" :question/worked-solution "First, note that we can write the equation of our surface as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{9}+\\frac{{z}^{2}}{4}-1=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, if we set $f(x,y,z)={x}^{2}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{9}+\\frac{{z}^{2}}{4}-1$, our surface can be viewed as the level surface $f(x,y,z)=0.$  \n\nA normal vector to the level surface that passes through the point $(0,0,2)$ can be found by computing $∇f(0,0,2).$ \n\nSo, we find the gradient and evaluate it at $(0,0,2):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(x,y,z) & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{2}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{9}+\\frac{{z}^{2}}{4}-1)i+\\frac{∂}{∂y}({x}^{2}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{9}+\\frac{{z}^{2}}{4}-1)j+\\frac{∂}{∂z}({x}^{2}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{9}+\\frac{{z}^{2}}{4}-1)k \\\\  & =2x\\text{ }i+\\frac{2y}{9}\\text{ }j+\\frac{z}{2}\\text{ }k \\\\ ∇f(0,0,2) & =2(0)\\text{ }i+\\frac{2(0)}{9}\\text{ }j+\\frac{(2)}{2}\\text{ }k \\\\  & =k \\\\  & =⟨0,0,1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nFinally, the vector form of the equation of the line that is parallel to $∇f(0,0,2)$ and passes through the point $(0,0,2)$ can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =⟨0,\\,0,\\,2⟩+t\\,∇f(0,0,2)=⟨0,\\,0,\\,2⟩+t\\,⟨0,\\,0,\\,1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-36754/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ce7d6557-ec20-5a40-b799-1a6a36cbe9e6"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-36754"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-71388/selection/78c897b0c43cf6fec0b2e19bcb7174179f28436f6056b451ad33f1dbe2e1605f" :answer/id #uuid "d383307d-39b2-5b44-a0bb-c6ed56a25ee2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y-x=1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-71388/selection/776f0796624aeb0fdb6a9591d89c0f7606b15e8a348d01f519cf2ab44f15d032" :answer/id #uuid "80488e4e-dae7-543e-92a0-ba47ca6c9b72" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x-y=1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-71388/selection/75ef4ad531ee85cdab4e659a5cbe87192f75d38c954d1b688963cc5fc87dc7b5" :answer/id #uuid "07199144-954c-5fb9-9281-fbd6b578758f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x-2y=1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-71388/selection/b4e9f88736f6235769f1115558fcd0c50567a236a153f886d5f704e64a825e07" :answer/id #uuid "327e391f-c2db-5954-82f9-0f504597cf37" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x+y=1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-71388/selection/f2a45832446b78a2400a4851897cf1bff9126f689b2ee41ef2b4345d40618936" :answer/id #uuid "24d75cf5-e417-5687-a614-6b11aab26878" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x+2y=1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-71388/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "52507be3-308b-5474-b419-8aabeb3a8d44" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-71388/selection/776f0796624aeb0fdb6a9591d89c0f7606b15e8a348d01f519cf2ab44f15d032" :answer-field/choices ["q-71388/selection/78c897b0c43cf6fec0b2e19bcb7174179f28436f6056b451ad33f1dbe2e1605f" "q-71388/selection/776f0796624aeb0fdb6a9591d89c0f7606b15e8a348d01f519cf2ab44f15d032" "q-71388/selection/75ef4ad531ee85cdab4e659a5cbe87192f75d38c954d1b688963cc5fc87dc7b5" "q-71388/selection/b4e9f88736f6235769f1115558fcd0c50567a236a153f886d5f704e64a825e07" "q-71388/selection/f2a45832446b78a2400a4851897cf1bff9126f689b2ee41ef2b4345d40618936"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-71388" :question/id #uuid "e82fe7da-02e3-534e-99f6-4b0ee233facf" :question/math-academy-id "q-71388" :question/problem "Consider the plane curve $2x+y-1=\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}}.$  Find the equation of the normal line to the curve at the point $(1,0).$" :question/worked-solution "First, we bring all variables to one side:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x+y-1 & =\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}} \\\\ -1 & =\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}}-2x-y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIf we set $f(x,y)=\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}}-2x-y$, our curve can be viewed as the level curve $f(x,y)=-1.$  \n\nA normal vector to the level curve that passes through the point $(1,0)$ can be found by computing $∇f(1,0).$ \n\nSo, we find the gradient and evaluate it at $(1,0):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(x,y) & ={f}_{x}(x,y)\\,i+{f}_{y}(x,y)\\,j \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}}-2x-y)\\,i+\\frac{∂}{∂y}(\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}}-2x-y)\\,j \\\\  & =(\\frac{x}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}}}-2)\\,i+(-\\frac{y}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}}}-1)\\,j \\\\ ∇f(1,0) & =(\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{1}^{2}-{0}^{2}}}-2)\\,i+(-\\frac{0}{\\sqrt{{1}^{2}-{0}^{2}}}-1)\\,j \\\\  & =-i-j \\\\  & =⟨-1,-1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, $∇f(1,0)=⟨-1,-1⟩$ is a normal vector to the curve at $(1,0).$\n\nFinally, the Cartesian equation of the line that is parallel to $v=⟨{v}_{x},{v}_{y}⟩$ and passes through the point $({x}_{0},{y}_{0})$ can be written as:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{x-{x}_{0}}{{v}_{x}} & =\\frac{y-{y}_{0}}{{v}_{y}} \\\\ \\frac{x-1}{-1} & =\\frac{y-0}{-1} \\\\ 1-x & =-y \\\\ x-y & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-71388/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3b2f7fab-cebe-519a-83e3-a0831cac289d"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-71388"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-71407/selection/06bf40f5b9eeb4992fa2a377b137e080af01c689da6dcb36d1382a9eedbe8f30" :answer/id #uuid "6b31a0be-80ae-57dc-9940-d27931890588" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "r=⟨-3,-4,1⟩+t\\,⟨\\frac{1}{2},1,3⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-71407/selection/269c123af6ae36024feba159134c72217e35ef2a7802ccca12091af6bbbba25d" :answer/id #uuid "b1f837b1-7d33-57e9-a9cb-31287c104b8f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "r=⟨3,-4,1⟩+t\\,⟨\\frac{1}{2},1,3⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-71407/selection/5ed43ba66786d5936490fbbe3dad5d448a587e07b6fd2a4dcb3c3ef3e179592f" :answer/id #uuid "12ea20d2-3502-57b7-9b33-7479f31d787e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "r=⟨\\frac{1}{2},1,3⟩+t\\,⟨3,-4,1⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-71407/selection/31db3834f30863a76832c6969b27251aba68465614cb0690b8612f0ad94e0cba" :answer/id #uuid "6a987c18-a4a8-520c-b8f6-674b3f53509a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "r=⟨\\frac{1}{2},1,3⟩+t\\,⟨3,4,1⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-71407/selection/9cdc76a743d9bf747902a130e1678d290b1791dd3996e65c4bf49eab26044c26" :answer/id #uuid "3c6490d1-5aa9-5055-a31d-9d46b58528f4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "r=⟨\\frac{1}{2},1,3⟩+t\\,⟨-3,-4,1⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-71407/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "447c3cd3-d9c5-5114-8434-345243d995fa" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-71407/selection/9cdc76a743d9bf747902a130e1678d290b1791dd3996e65c4bf49eab26044c26" :answer-field/choices ["q-71407/selection/06bf40f5b9eeb4992fa2a377b137e080af01c689da6dcb36d1382a9eedbe8f30" "q-71407/selection/269c123af6ae36024feba159134c72217e35ef2a7802ccca12091af6bbbba25d" "q-71407/selection/5ed43ba66786d5936490fbbe3dad5d448a587e07b6fd2a4dcb3c3ef3e179592f" "q-71407/selection/31db3834f30863a76832c6969b27251aba68465614cb0690b8612f0ad94e0cba" "q-71407/selection/9cdc76a743d9bf747902a130e1678d290b1791dd3996e65c4bf49eab26044c26"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-71407" :question/id #uuid "ca7dad4d-8007-5c21-9019-38d66b5366c7" :question/math-academy-id "q-71407" :question/problem "Find a vector equation of the normal line to the surface $z=2{x}^{2}+2{y}^{2}+x$ at the point $(\\frac{1}{2},1,3).$" :question/worked-solution "First, we bring all variables to one side:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z & =2{x}^{2}+2{y}^{2}+x \\\\ z-2{x}^{2}-2{y}^{2}-x & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIf we set $f(x,y,z)=z-2{x}^{2}-2{y}^{2}-x$, our surface can be viewed as the level surface $f(x,y,z)=0.$ \n\nA normal vector to the level surface that passes through the point $(\\frac{1}{2},1,3)$ can be found by computing $∇f(\\frac{1}{2},1,3).$ \n\nSo, we find the gradient and evaluate it at $(\\frac{1}{2},1,3):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(x,y,z) & ={f}_{x}(x,y,z)\\,i+{f}_{y}(x,y,z)\\text{ }j+{f}_{z}(x,y,z)\\text{ }k \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(z-2{x}^{2}-2{y}^{2}-x)i+\\frac{∂}{∂y}(z-2{x}^{2}-2{y}^{2}-x)j+\\frac{∂}{∂z}(z-2{x}^{2}-2{y}^{2}-x)k \\\\  & =(-4x-1)\\text{ }i-4y\\text{ }j+k \\\\ ∇f(\\frac{1}{2},1,3) & =(-4(\\frac{1}{2})-1)\\,i-4(1)\\text{ }j+k \\\\  & =-3\\,i-4\\,j+k \\\\  & =⟨-3,-4,1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the vector equation of the line that is parallel to $∇f(\\frac{1}{2},1,3)$ and passes through the point $(\\frac{1}{2},1,3)$ can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =⟨\\frac{1}{2},1,3⟩+t\\,∇f(\\frac{1}{2},1,3)=⟨\\frac{1}{2},1,3⟩+t\\,⟨-3,-4,1⟩,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-71407/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ce7d6557-ec20-5a40-b799-1a6a36cbe9e6"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-71407"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-130718/selection/94ddeef695568db5bf0697aedf5093daaa8d5222ef25bce0c4fdada5116ef593" :answer/id #uuid "24db7740-142f-5ff4-ad09-89cffbccbd4c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x-y-2=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-130718/selection/6af38187ed65b459f5aab3f5ee55ffc405508126e60841860456a931bb98a267" :answer/id #uuid "5b2811c8-62aa-5a93-8981-18721a20ad59" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x+3y-6=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-130718/selection/b2ca7f8ef614dff191dc6bead7e897758d711189c06399a3527ec8584edb4db9" :answer/id #uuid "08936e67-0d0d-5760-a873-7da74707acef" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x-3y=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-130718/selection/7845fb55d27454e306181898eeddd164e7374d7249dea3cb5c41c585387b7cad" :answer/id #uuid "83eed442-106f-5182-8a04-9b0e401c10cd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x+y-4=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-130718/selection/6993e079ff6c62c022e01fbebbd64cb5afc95a2788b0705de16fb3a9978ce034" :answer/id #uuid "76573843-ec78-585b-af82-bae778b83009" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2x+y-7=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-130718/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "6f798868-eff2-5e73-9471-09264f27a8c3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-130718/selection/7845fb55d27454e306181898eeddd164e7374d7249dea3cb5c41c585387b7cad" :answer-field/choices ["q-130718/selection/94ddeef695568db5bf0697aedf5093daaa8d5222ef25bce0c4fdada5116ef593" "q-130718/selection/6af38187ed65b459f5aab3f5ee55ffc405508126e60841860456a931bb98a267" "q-130718/selection/b2ca7f8ef614dff191dc6bead7e897758d711189c06399a3527ec8584edb4db9" "q-130718/selection/7845fb55d27454e306181898eeddd164e7374d7249dea3cb5c41c585387b7cad" "q-130718/selection/6993e079ff6c62c022e01fbebbd64cb5afc95a2788b0705de16fb3a9978ce034"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-130718" :question/id #uuid "185f66f3-9fba-5841-9ae6-a31944a1af0d" :question/math-academy-id "q-130718" :question/problem "Consider the plane curve ${x}^{2}-3{y}^{2}=6.$  Find the equation of the normal line to the curve at the point $(3,1).$" :question/worked-solution "If we set $f(x,y)={x}^{2}-3{y}^{2},$ our curve can be viewed as the level curve $f(x,y)=6.$  \n\nA normal vector to the level curve that passes through the point $(3,1)$ can be found by computing $∇f(3,1).$ \n\nSo, we find the gradient and evaluate it at $(3,1):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(x,y) & ={f}_{x}(x,y)\\,i+{f}_{y}(x,y)\\,j \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{2}-3{y}^{2})\\,i+\\frac{∂}{∂y}({x}^{2}-3{y}^{2})\\,j \\\\  & =2x\\,i-6y\\,j \\\\ ∇f(3,1) & =2(3)\\,i-6(1)\\,j \\\\  & =6\\,i-6\\,j \\\\  & =⟨6,-6⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, $∇f(3,1)=⟨6,-6⟩$ is a normal vector to the curve at $(3,1).$\n\nFinally, the Cartesian equation of the line that is parallel to $v=⟨{v}_{x},{v}_{y}⟩$ and passes through the point $({x}_{0},{y}_{0})$ can be written as:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{x-{x}_{0}}{{v}_{x}} & =\\frac{y-{y}_{0}}{{v}_{y}} \\\\ \\frac{x-3}{6} & =\\frac{y-1}{(-6)} \\\\ -6(x-3) & =6(y-1) \\\\ -(x-3) & =y-1 \\\\ -x+3 & =y-1 \\\\ x+y-4 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-130718/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3b2f7fab-cebe-519a-83e3-a0831cac289d"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-130718"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-131115/selection/17b1d8fe55ca783a7b810a3ea165a07c8c8db238aba0dc8a61508163fe6e0e58" :answer/id #uuid "4dbaef38-07e5-5120-922c-f92b0bf12ef8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}\\,i-j+k" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-131115/selection/6fb422a0878cc254ec63e6b53e4eeaf925a3e7b2206a78cc8e809b2e771b1da0" :answer/id #uuid "688b0570-33d1-547f-88ac-8355397694b7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "i+\\frac{1}{4}\\,j+\\frac{1}{2}\\,k" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-131115/selection/fc1bb788a729c1d76e5ac641e62149cc0ecd5b130958a664ef8cdb909246f434" :answer/id #uuid "5f0a8753-ae01-5ea7-a98c-333a2b9c7968" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}\\,i+\\frac{1}{2}\\,j+k" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-131115/selection/023dd2916e906cdec5f3e1363d2f872fde95b755cbfb94da813775ceebff5684" :answer/id #uuid "b295344e-e699-5f9b-973c-133bb94797ac" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}\\,i+\\frac{3}{2}\\,j+\\frac{1}{2}\\,k" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-131115/selection/3d2f1e9a3df0e80425f1ef82cbcda28ef5b2ed58e9853cdc86ac40c560c05180" :answer/id #uuid "8184a3fd-fd88-58f2-baeb-76fb0f7d30ca" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "i+\\frac{1}{2}\\,j+k" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-131115/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "84f8131f-da98-5ca7-8fec-b89d5f9e624f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-131115/selection/3d2f1e9a3df0e80425f1ef82cbcda28ef5b2ed58e9853cdc86ac40c560c05180" :answer-field/choices ["q-131115/selection/17b1d8fe55ca783a7b810a3ea165a07c8c8db238aba0dc8a61508163fe6e0e58" "q-131115/selection/6fb422a0878cc254ec63e6b53e4eeaf925a3e7b2206a78cc8e809b2e771b1da0" "q-131115/selection/fc1bb788a729c1d76e5ac641e62149cc0ecd5b130958a664ef8cdb909246f434" "q-131115/selection/023dd2916e906cdec5f3e1363d2f872fde95b755cbfb94da813775ceebff5684" "q-131115/selection/3d2f1e9a3df0e80425f1ef82cbcda28ef5b2ed58e9853cdc86ac40c560c05180"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-131115" :question/id #uuid "c83000c4-b29e-5b4d-9073-cd5d94e04a02" :question/math-academy-id "q-131115" :question/problem "For the function $f(x,y,z)=\\sqrt{xy}+\\sqrt{yz},$ find a vector that's perpendicular to the level surface that passes through the point where $(x,y,z)=(1,4,1).$" :question/worked-solution "A normal vector to the level surface that passes through the point where $(x,y,z)=(1,4,1)$ can be found by computing \n$∇f(1,4,1).$ \n\nSo, we first find the gradient and evaluate it at $(x,y,z)=(1,4,1):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(x,y,z) & ={f}_{x}(x,y,z)\\,i+{f}_{y}(x,y,z)\\,j+{f}_{z}(x,y,z)\\,k \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\sqrt{xy}+\\sqrt{yz})\\,i+\\frac{∂}{∂y}(\\sqrt{xy}+\\sqrt{yz}+)\\,j+\\frac{∂}{∂z}(\\sqrt{xy}+\\sqrt{yz})\\,k \\\\  & =\\frac{y}{2\\sqrt{xy}}\\,i+(\\frac{x}{2\\sqrt{xy}}+\\frac{z}{2\\sqrt{yz}})j+\\frac{y}{2\\sqrt{yz}}\\,k \\\\ ∇f(1,4,1) & =\\frac{4}{2\\sqrt{1(4)}}\\,i+(\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{1(4)}}+\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{4(1)}})j+\\frac{4}{2\\sqrt{4(1)}}\\,k \\\\  & =i+\\frac{1}{2}\\,j+k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $i+\\frac{1}{2}\\,j+k$ is perpendicular to the level surface that passes through the point where $(x,y,z)=(1,4,1).$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-131115/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4516cb28-0fc0-5c15-b9b2-747c3827e189"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-131115"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
